# The Amazon SNS-compatible publish/subscribe service (services/sns/,
# .kiro/specs/sns-compatible-notifications/). Sourced from the top-level
# Kconfig's "Service Modules" menu.

config SNS
	bool "Amazon SNS-compatible publish/subscribe service"
	default n
	depends on OPENSSL
	help
	  Builds the services/sns/ module: an Amazon SNS-compatible
	  publish/subscribe service that unmodified AWS SDKs and the AWS CLI
	  can point at to create topics, subscribe SQS queues, HTTP/HTTPS
	  endpoints and email addresses, and publish. Each topic's messages
	  commit through Kythira's Raft groups into a publish log in the
	  record segment store, which delivery workers read. So far the
	  module holds the pinned botocore model, the generated operation
	  table, the coverage check and the sns_node placeholder (task 1);
	  the gateway, front end, topic state machine and delivery follow.
	  It needs IAM's core SigV4 and authorizer headers, not the IAM
	  module. OpenSSL is needed for SigV4 and message signatures. Off by
	  default like every new module (services/README.md). See
	  .kiro/specs/sns-compatible-notifications/.
